    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive core is headlined by **Mickey Moniak** (74.73) and **Corbin Carroll** (72.25). **Mickey Moniak** presents the highest ceiling of the day, buoyed by a significant +14% dynamic platoon advantage and a favorable park factor, making him an elite play against Gray. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** remains a priority start; his elite sprint speed is a cornerstone of our strategy, and facing Leahy provides the exact environment needed for him to maximize his stolen base potential and run-scoring output. **Josh Naylor** (69.39) rounds out our top-tier trio, benefiting from a high-efficiency matchup against Keller, whose xERA of 4.45 allows for high-leverage outcomes in the middle of our order.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was keeping **Zach McKinstry** on the bench with a 51.70 score. While his platoon advantage against a lefty like Rod\u00f3n is enticing, he was narrowly edged out by the higher floor provided by **Alex Freeland** and **Max Muncy**. **Freeland**\u2019s superior SP skill metrics (+19%) and switch-hitting versatility ultimately secured him the MI slot over the bench alternatives. We are closely monitoring the status of **James Wood**; while his 55.98 score is solid, his matchup against a high-velocity, elite-holding pitcher like Luzardo presents a situational risk to his stolen base floor that we are watching closely. Owners should be wary of any last-minute lineup adjustments, as the lack of confirmed confirmation for several spots could shift our efficiency scores as we approach first pitch.",
